# Quiz Scenario: Simple 3-vertex rescue problem
# Vertices: loc1, loc2, loc3
# People at: loc2, loc3
# Kit at: loc1
# Flooded edges: 1-2
# Agent starts at: loc1
# Goal: rescue all people

# Initial State
At(agent, loc1, s0)
HasPeople(loc2, s0)
HasPeople(loc3, s0)
HasKit(loc1, s0)
~Equipped(agent, s0)

# Flooded edges
Flooded(loc1, loc2)
~Flooded(loc1, loc3)
~Flooded(loc2, loc3)

# Traversal preconditions
~Flooded(loc1, loc2) | Equipped(agent, s) | ~CanTraverse(loc1, loc2, s)
CanTraverse(loc1, loc3, s)
CanTraverse(loc2, loc3, s)

# Effects: traverse and rescue
~At(agent, loc1, s) | ~CanTraverse(loc1, loc2, s) | At(agent, loc2, result(s))
~At(agent, loc1, s) | ~CanTraverse(loc1, loc3, s) | At(agent, loc3, result(s))
~At(agent, loc2, s) | ~CanTraverse(loc2, loc3, s) | At(agent, loc3, result(s))

~At(agent, loc2, s) | ~HasPeople(loc2, s) | ~HasPeople(loc2, result(s))
~At(agent, loc3, s) | ~HasPeople(loc3, s) | ~HasPeople(loc3, result(s))

# Equip at loc1
~At(agent, loc1, s) | ~HasKit(loc1, s) | Equipped(agent, equip_result(s))

# Goal negated (someone still not rescued)
HasPeople(loc_unsaved, final_s)
